<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <!-- DISTRIBUTION entitlements: LDA.entitlements plus the three RESTRICTED
       keys that Touch ID protection of the keychain keys needs.

       Why a second file, and why these three are NOT in LDA.entitlements:
       a restricted entitlement is honoured only when an embedded Developer ID
       provisioning profile grants it. A binary that CLAIMS one without the
       profile is killed at exec (SIGKILL, exit 137) before it prints a line;
       measured three runs, control run fine. The ad hoc dev build has no
       profile, so it must never carry these, and package-app.sh only signs
       with this file when CODESIGN_IDENTITY and PROVISIONING_PROFILE are both
       set and the profile has been copied into the bundle first.

       Why Touch ID needs them: a keychain item with a user-presence access
       control lives in the data-protection keychain, and macOS builds that
       keychain's list of access groups from the app's code-signing
       entitlements (TN3137). Without an application identifier there is no
       group, SecItemAdd returns errSecMissingEntitlement (-34018), and the app
       silently falls back to an unprotected key. That is what shipped for
       every release before this file existed.

       The profile (portal name "LDA Developer ID", App ID
       B53GT262L4.com.haotianyi.LDA) allowlists keychain-access-groups as
       B53GT262L4.*, so the specific group claimed below is within it.
       PackagingEntitlementsTests pins this file as the base file plus exactly
       these three keys, with values derived from Info.plist and the team, so
       neither file can drift from the other unnoticed. -->

  <key>com.apple.security.app-sandbox</key>
  <true/>
  <key>com.apple.security.files.user-selected.read-write</key>
  <true/>
  <key>com.apple.security.files.bookmarks.app-scope</key>
  <true/>
  <key>com.apple.security.network.client</key>
  <true/>

  <key>com.apple.application-identifier</key>
  <string>B53GT262L4.com.haotianyi.LDA</string>
  <key>com.apple.developer.team-identifier</key>
  <string>B53GT262L4</string>
  <key>keychain-access-groups</key>
  <array>
    <string>B53GT262L4.com.haotianyi.LDA</string>
  </array>
</dict>
</plist>
